  "findings": [
    "UPA1-UPA4: unramified CM and split-place consequences use the original level inclusions. Inertia at every prolongation, including transported valuations, lies in the closed image of the candidate kernel, so the original normal closure is killed without assuming that candidate subgroup normal. Actual quotient surjectivity, quotient topology, invariant subspaces, and unchanged polarization matrix are all checked.",
    "UPA5-UPA7: Satake normalization matches the original all-j Hecke polynomial, including j=0 and j>n. HasSatGL is explicit on all nonzero fixed vectors and every uniformizer. Every-IsRecT GUA12 normalization and the q^((1-n)/2) twist give the required characteristic polynomial on inverse arithmetic Frobenius; the original inertia comparison is supplied explicitly through UPA9.",
    "UPA8-UPA9: global characters kill Weil commutators and activate exactly the conditional WDT equality. Zero monodromy yields an open killed inertia subgroup; finite-order matrices and the commuting semisimple/nilpotent witness recover literal inertia before applying the same type intertwiner. Coefficient transport uses only the algebraic fixed iota.",
    "UPA10-UPA12: distinct restrictions to units force the original plain-toral support clauses. Reversed-negative dual weights give precisely lowW+i, with every period-induced embedding extended to the actual completion. LocGlobT plus the retained plain-toral Hodge implication supplies every DRat bridge/test and hence the full AtLT, retaining its every-IsRecT and AbW quantifiers.",
    "UPA13-UPA16: one component family and one global R are retained through descent and every conclusion. Checked all sixteen literal PartAltAlt fields and all four UnitaryPointProperties fields, including every Teichmuller family, same polarization matrix, conditional cusp conclusion, all split local components, all outside-level unramified places and the exact Kc(1) distinguished fixed space. The strengthened original partX_alt tuple and projected partU_alt match.",
    "UPA17: an arbitrary original TypeForAlt yields open integral kernel by a Teichmuller family and injective scalar extension. ADP12 then supplies the actual function-space decomposition; zero parts contribute zero, nonzero parts are the constructed original parts. All weight, basis, level, depth and function inputs remain quantified.",
    "UPA18: the exact hAut supplier previously retained by AFS22 is now constructed. The source zero-module branch and original nonzero Hecke kernel branch give density of the same ideal J, with the original V.Sprime=s.S hypothesis and all source coefficient inputs preserved."
  ],
